{"title":"Career Roadmap: Cultural Researcher","role":"Cultural Researcher","summary":"A Cultural Researcher studies cultural practices, communities, identities, historical traditions, media, language, heritage and social change.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Digital Humanities / Cultural Studies"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build expertise in cultural research, humanities methodology, archival research, digital humanities, cultural documentation, data analysis and evidence-based interpretation"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Cultural Researcher studies cultural practices, communities, identities, historical traditions, media, language, heritage and social change."},{"type":"p","text":"Research areas can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cultural history"},{"text":"Popular culture"},{"text":"Folklore"},{"text":"Oral traditions"},{"text":"Literature"},{"text":"Language and identity"},{"text":"Religion and culture"},{"text":"Museums and heritage"},{"text":"Digital culture"},{"text":"Media and society"},{"text":"Migration and diaspora"},{"text":"Indigenous/local knowledge"},{"text":"Cultural policy"},{"text":"Creative industries"},{"text":"Community studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Digital Humanities specialization adds computational and digital methods to traditional humanities research. This can include digital archives, text analysis, GIS, databases, visualization, digitization and computational research."},{"type":"p","text":"The target title \"Cultural Researcher\" is usually reached through research-assistant, project-assistant or research-associate roles, with postgraduate research training strongly beneficial for long-term research careers."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","P